 ## When to use Mastra Code
 
+- **Long-running projects**: Mastra Code's persistent threads and [Observational Memory](https://mastra.ai/docs/memory/observational-memory) make it ideal for ongoing projects where context builds up over time.
+- **No compaction headaches**: With Observational Memory, you never have to worry about losing important context due to token limits. Mastra Code automatically manages what to remember and what to forget.
 - **Day-to-day coding**: Ask questions about your codebase, make edits, run tests, and manage Git.
 - **Code exploration**: Use Plan mode to analyze architecture and create implementation plans before writing code.
 - **Quick lookups**: Switch to Fast mode for brief answers and small edits with minimal latency.
